Package: mortensor
Title: Cause-Specific Mortality Forecasting with Tensor Decomposition
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Karl", "Emmert-Fees", email = "karl.emmert-fees@tum.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A modular toolkit for cause-specific mortality forecasting using
    Tucker tensor decomposition, compositional data analysis (CoDa), and
    ensemble time-series methods. Provides a step-by-step workflow
    (calibrate -> forecast -> add_pi -> disaggregate) with S3 classes for
    mortality data, calibrations, and forecasts. Includes Tucker3/Tucker4
    decomposition, Lee-Carter, FDM, StMoMo, ARIMA, ETS, and random walk with
    drift models; BIC/AIC and cross-validation rank selection; bootstrap and
    GAM-Bayes prediction intervals; proper scoring rules (MASE, CRPS, interval
    score, WIS); WLS-based multi-disease reconciliation; age disaggregation via
    Hyman+Kannisto, Natural+Gompertz, and GAM methods; and standard abridged
    life tables. Designed for stratified mortality data (e.g. by sex and
    deprivation quintile).
